  "preamble": "Lowering of [ə] to the open back vowel [ɑ]. In the prehistory of Proto-Germanic, the schwa that developed from a PIE laryngeal between consonants was lost when unstressed between consonants and otherwise became /ɑ/, merging with the vowel that continued PIE *a and *o (*ph₂tḗr > *fədēr > *fadēr 'father').",
